; A program that needs a **fourth** walk: `two-rounds.z80` one level deeper.
;
; Three forward `br`s, nested, each brought into range only by the shrinking
; of the one inside it. `inner` fits at once; `middle` is one byte out until
; `inner` shrinks; `outer` is two bytes out until both have.
;
;   walk 1   everything forward is assumed long
;              br outer at 0, br middle at 3, 122 nops, br inner at 128,
;              inner and outer at 131, middle at 133, and the program is 134
;   walk 2   outer: 131 - 2 = 129, out   middle: 133 - 5 = 128, out
;              inner fits: inner and outer at 130, middle at 132, 133 bytes
;   walk 3   outer: 130 - 2 = 128, out   middle: 132 - 5 = 127, fits
;              inner and outer at 129, middle at 131: 132 bytes
;   walk 4   outer: 129 - 2 = 127, fits, and everything after it moves one
;              down: 131 bytes, which is the minimum
;   walk 5   nothing moves, so the driver stops
        br outer
        br middle
